# Workflow: HUMAN-DOCS-GATE

Purpose:
  Define the human documentation gate — the checkpoint ensuring every
  code change is accompanied by human-readable documentation that
  explains WHY and WHAT, not just HOW. Code says HOW; documentation
  explains WHY + WHAT. Documentation is project-specific and
  generated from the project context.

Owns:
  Human documentation gate
  Documentation template (project-based)
  Code-to-docs mapping verification

DocumentationGate:

  definition: checkpoint between DOCUMENTING and KNOWLEDGE GATE
              stages (bax execution-loop.sdd)
  position: after Done Proof, before Knowledge Gate
  prerequisite: Done Proof must pass (bax DONE-PROOF.sdd)

  principle:
    Code says HOW.
    Documentation explains WHY + WHAT.

  requirement: every code change MUST have a human-docs-gate entry

HumanDocsTemplate:

  format:
    project: <project_name>
    changed: <feature/component/module>
    why: <business or technical reason for the change>
    how: <mechanism: list of technical details>
    affected:
      - <affected_components>
    references:
      - <@knowledge_ref>*

  Example:
    project:
      payment-service
    changed:
      refund
    why:
      prevent duplicate provider refunds
    how:
      idempotency key
      transaction
      outbox
    affected:
      PaymentService
      RefundRepository
      Refund API
    references:
      @payment.idempotency
      @decision.outbox

BadDocumentation:

  anti_patterns:
    - "This function calls Refund." (just restates code)
    - copy-pasted docstrings that repeat signature
    - "The code below does X" followed by code (tautology)
    - implementation details without business context

  rule: [HD1] Documentation MUST NOT restate what the code literally does.

GoodDocumentation:

  example:
    "Refund operation is protected against duplicate execution because
    external payment providers may retry requests. The system persists
    the idempotency key before processing the financial mutation."

  quality:
    - explains business/technical reason (WHY)
    - summarizes scope and mechanism (WHAT)
    - links to decisions and knowledge artifacts

CodeDocsMapping:

  definition: every code change traces to a human docs entry
  verification:
    - docs/ has 1:1 mapping to .sdd/project/
    - every modified source file maps to a documentation section
    - documentation review is a required gate

  rule: [HD2] If documentation does not exist, the task is NOT
        Engineering Done.

ReviewResult:

  PASS               — documentation explains WHY + WHAT
  CHANGES_REQUIRED   — documentation restates code or misses context
  BLOCKED            — documentation missing for a changed component
  ESCALATE           — documentation conflict or ambiguity

  flow:
    PASS -> Knowledge Gate
    CHANGES_REQUIRED -> update docs -> re-review
    BLOCKED -> document the missing piece -> re-review
    ESCALATE -> human clarification -> resolve

ProjectScope:

  rule: [HD3] Documentation is project_name-based — generated from
        the specific project's context, conventions, and architecture.
  rule: [HD4] Project-level docs take precedence over generic templates.
  rule: [HD5] Documentation MUST reference @knowledge and @decision artifacts.

Rules:

  [HD1] Documentation MUST NOT restate code — it explains WHY + WHAT.
  [HD2] Missing documentation = task NOT Engineering Done.
  [HD3] Documentation is project_name-specific.
  [HD4] Project-level docs take precedence over generic knowledge.
  [HD5] Every changed component MUST have a documentation entry.
  [HD6] Documentation MUST link to @decision and @knowledge references.
  [HD7] Documentation review is a required gate — not optional.
  [HD8] Bad documentation (restatement of code) requires rewrite.
  [HD9] Documentation is validated alongside Done Proof (bax DONE-PROOF.sdd).
  [HD10] Human-readable docs provide the WHY context for future engineers.

Navigation:

  ExecutionLoop: @execution-loop.sdd
  DoneProof: @../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd
  LearningGate: @learning-gate.sdd
  KnowledgeModel: @../concepts/INDEX.sdd
  Decisions: @../decisions/INDEX.sdd
  ProjectsDocs: @../projects/{project_name}/docs/INDEX.sdd
  TasksIndex: @../tasks/INDEX.sdd

State: +
